152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (If electricity demand is to follow the forecasted growth, from 10-15%, there is a strong chance the power grid market will not be able to keep up. Power grids are essential for data center use, amongst other things, as they are the vessels that deliver electricity from power plants to data centers, homes, businesses, and more across the nation. They both generate and distribute electricity, and areas would not be able to get power without the infrastructure. Will the world be able to keep up with the incredibly fast depletion of energy that data centers bring on? And will AI and data center progress face a rude awakening as the reality sets in that faster data centers and GPUs come with a hefty energy price?)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
